WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.440
I, Akeno Mihoshi, am back from my school trip!

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.280
White Friend, Hakkatei Chocolate, Butter Sandwich, Local Kichy,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.280
[Note: White Friend = White Lover, a famous Japanese chocolate brand,
Hakkatei Chocolate = Rokkei Chocolate, and Kichy = the Hello Kitty brand.]

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.040
wooden carvings, key rings, Hokkaido rocks, and something I bought especially for you...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.750
Now, go ahead and inhale.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.340
Does it smell like Hokkaido?

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.420
No!

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:38.890
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.740
Just one word is fine.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.570
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.700
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.790
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.920
Your answers will...

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.920
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.330
Even more...

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.210
Like fireworks...

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:17.430
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:24.430
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:30.980
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:36.110
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.080
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:50.290
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.550
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.520
All right, let's go!

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:11.060
Yup!

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.400
Well then, take care on your way home.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.400
Will do!

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:16.440
Oh!

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.070
Sou-nii!

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:20.820
It's about tomorrow.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.990
Can we still go as planned?

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.740
Sure, but aren't you tired from your school trip?

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:25.870
I'm fine!

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.460
Well, I'll see you at the station plaza at 11 o'clock, okay?

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.130
Hey! Hey! Is something happening tomorrow?

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:32.210
I don't know.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.250
Why are you asking me anyway?

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.460
There's no school tomorrow...

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.800
...and at midday?

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:39.630
Isn't that suspicious?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:40.890
Not really.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.260
They've known each other for a long time.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.850
Oh, maybe Sayo-senpai's going too?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.940
What? Tomorrow?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.100
I don't have any plans for tomorrow.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.480
It <i>is</i> suspicious.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.480
It <i>is</i> suspicious.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.190
Well, it doesn't concern me...

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.400
As a side note, I-

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.990
We don't want to know your schedule, President!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.420
Why are you guys here?!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.340
I'm here for your sake.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.090
I'm here because Edogawa-kun asked me.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:26.140
T-To avoid any misunderstandings, I'm just on my way back from the bookstore...

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.220
Now, now.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.810
Oh, look! She's here.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.520
This <i>is</i> a date!

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.060
It's so obviously a date!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.690
Hm... I'm starting to think that they'd make a good couple.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.200
Well, I think I'll be going...

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.030
Hey, you!

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.990
Hey, you!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:29.450
After following them this far, we <i>must</i> find out where they're going!

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.540
What?!

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.880
I wonder where they're going.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.350
Where are we?

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.350
Let's see...

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.900
P-President?!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:58.900
Oumi-san?!

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.980
Quiet! Quiet!

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.570
W-Where are they going?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.070
No! I want to check them out too!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.490
I said, quiet!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.950
If I knew that this was going to happen, I would've listened to his schedule yesterday.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.370
There's nothing we can do; focus on the one we have now.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:28.090
But you know, Souma-sensei somehow understands her.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:29.640
Does it bother you?

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.600
No, it's nothing like that-

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.350
Sayo-senpai?!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.430
Why are you here?!

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.900
I was at the station plaza picking up some photographs when...

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.730
...I saw you three behaving suspiciously, so I followed you.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.990
So, you were watching us?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.190
We're sorry...

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.530
Honestly, what were you all thinking-

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.370
Quiet!

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.950
Come on, we're getting off.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.380
W-Where are we?

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.050
Rather...

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.470
...why these pairings?

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.050
Hey, guys...

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:09.970
Huh?

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.560
What's wrong, Sou-nii?

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.600
It's nothing. It was just my imagination.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.610
Phew... So they were just passing through.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.400
Hey, guys-

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.530
They're going further in.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:32.740
It's hard to walk on this path in high-heels...

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.200
Are we there yet?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.410
I think we're almost there.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.050
Papa, I've come to visit you this year too.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.230
That hurt...

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:01.690
Saku-chan... All of you...

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.280
Honestly, you surprised me.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.530
How long have you been there?

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.910
If you'd told me, we could have-

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:15.620
I had...

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.450
I had no idea.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.080
Why did he....

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.510
He died in a car accident on his way home from a stargazing session.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.390
It happened around this time of the year.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.600
I thought I'd join her this year.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.560
Apparently, her mother's too busy and her schedule won't allow her to come.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.400
Mihoshi told me that she's been coming here by herself over the past few years.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.070
I'm sorry for surprising everyone.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.950
I missed my chance to tell you all...

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.950
But I'm sure he's happy...

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.710
...to see Saku-chan... to see everyone.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.920
But he was a really generous man.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.510
He used to joke a lot; I was never sure if he was telling the truth or lying.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.050
Sometimes, he played with me and Mihoshi.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.850
He loved Mihoshi and was always looking up at the sky.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:23.890
Why?

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:31.150
I thought that even after I left, this city would remain unchanged, continuing on as normal.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:36.530
That I would be the only one to disappear, and everything else would remain the same...

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:38.580
Why?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.080
I wonder why.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.540
It's what everyone asks themselves.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:49.840
But you know, Mihoshi-chan told him how she saw shooting stars with you this year.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.710
That she was really happy.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:58.720
I think she's really happy that everyone was with her today.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.600
Oh, it's so dark now.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.310
Mihoshi, do you want to drop by my place?

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:07.100
Sure!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.530
It looks like the weather will be nice tomorrow too.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.040
See you tomorrow!

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:46.560
Really, that mock exam I took yesterday was so hard.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.980
It's the first one I've ever taken outside of school.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:53.900
The prep school Oumi-kun introduced me to gave us a mock exam.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.650
Who's the guy next to Oumi-san?!

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.700
Oumi-san!

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.490
So that must be what they call the famous entrance examination war.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.370
I don't think so...

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.330
Wow! Look at these! They're amazing!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:11.630
It's a photograph of Mercury crossing the Sun's surface that Oumi-san gave our president yesterday.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.550
All right! We're going to do our best too!

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.010
Right, Saku-chan?

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:21.890
Sorry, I'm late-

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.560
Hey, what are you-

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.270
Hime-chan?!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.690
I've got to go now.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.440
Me too! Me too!

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:40.200
Saku-chan? Edogawa-kun?

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.700
We can't blame them.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.410
After all, they only found out about it yesterday.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.760
What am I doing?

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:02.600
It's not as though I want to avoid her, but I don't know what to do when she smiles at me.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.390
Mii-chan's always smiling.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.850
Right now, what can I do?

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:14.770
Well then, please take this home and give it some thought.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:15.820
That is all.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.450
That took a while, didn't it?

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:26.370
Yes, it did.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:31.870
What's wrong?

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.960
You look like you've forgotten something important; I've never seen you look like that before.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.300
It's nothing.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:43.760
I should have given him the souvenir from my school trip two days ago.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.850
It was just one night, but I feel like I've missed the perfect opportunity.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.060
Haraguchi.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:52.940
Yes?

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:58.030
If you give a guy a bookmark as a souvenir, it doesn't have any special meaning, right?

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:58.570
What?

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.700
It's nothing. Forget it.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.660
The longer I take, the harder it'll be to give to him.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.830
That's what I read somewhere.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:12.370
I'll give it to him as soon as possible.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.880
It's just a souvenir; it's nothing special.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:19.880
What's going on?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.470
Oh, Kotodzuka-senpai! Perfect timing.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.010
The Astronomy Club's acting strange!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.060
The Astronomy Club has always been strange.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:30.850
No, it's different this time.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:34.520
Ooyagi-kun and Mihoshi-san are suddenly all lovey-dovey!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.360
Saku-chan, I'm cheerful!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.310
Come on, Mihoshi.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.990
Come on, we're going back to our classroom.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.240
Saku-chan!

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:48.780
Did you see that? Did you see that?

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:51.830
His ennui eyes when he looks at Mihoshi-senpai.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.750
He never looked at her like that before.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:54.710
I see.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.880
See what I mean? It's even harder to give it to him now.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.920
If I don't manage to give it to him today, I'll give up.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:16.730
Good afternoon. Kotodzuka-senpai, are you here on Student Council business?

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.770
Can I speak to you? Um...

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.190
Watch out!

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:28.280
I'm sorry, President!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.030
A-Are you okay?

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.750
Yes... but I can't find my glasses.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:41.670
I-I'm very sorry.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.840
We're very sorry!

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.380
Don't worry. I'll be fine.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.430
I've got a second pair at home.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.640
Watch out!

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:00.190
Both Yoshinari-san and Izumi-san have already left...

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.860
I'll be fine.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.610
I'm fine going home by myself.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.490
Um... you're talking to the bust of our principle.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:05.940
What?!

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:13.490
I wonder if Akeno will get the wrong idea if she sees us together.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.080
Huh?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:16.370
Let's see...

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.790
You went to the same elementary school as Mihoshi, so you must take the bus that goes past the apartment complex, right?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:20.380
Yes, that's right.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:24.760
I used to live near the apartment complex too.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:28.090
I used to live in the same apartment complex as Mii-chan-as Mihoshi.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.260
Look! Ito's Bookstore is still here!

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.890
What? This place is now an apartment complex?!

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.690
Wow! The playground toys are tiny!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.110
I'm sorry.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:47.690
I just couldn't help myself.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.740
Oh, I can't see well, that's all.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:56.200
I haven't been to any places from my childhood since I've come back.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.210
I wonder why I didn't come here earlier...

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.210
Why did I leave this city?

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.590
I'm glad my glasses are broken.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.890
Here. It's a souvenir from Hokkaido.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.930
It's a thank you for helping during the Cultural Festival.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:24.190
Although there are a lot of things I don't know, if it's fine with you, I'll be happy to listen to your worries...

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.940
I don't want to see his expression right now...

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.320
...as your Student Council President.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.160
Kotodzuka-senpai...

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.620
...that's Papo-kun.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.580
[Note: Papo-kun is a reference to Tokyo's Police mascot, Pipo-kun.]

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.620
Huh? Kotodzuka-senpai?

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:39.370
Ooyagi-kun!

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.410
What a coincidence!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.880
What happened to your glasses?!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.290
What are you two doing here?

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:49.510
Then, we'll walk her home.

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.090
See you tomorrow.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:07.690
Kotodzuka-senpai!

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.660
Will you listen to what's troubling me?

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.870
Saku-chan's not coming today either...

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.960
We all studied together on our previous exams...

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.420
I wonder what's wrong.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:34.800
I wonder if Saku-chan's mad at me because I didn't tell him.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:39.390
I told him that I was happy and that he needn't worry about me. Maybe my words didn't reach him.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:40.680
Now, now.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.350
How should you act if you don't want to worry people?

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:44.730
Happy!

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:45.940
Good girl.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:54.780
Really?

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:59.580
Yes. They will let you use it, however, there will be a few restrictions.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:02.750
Thank you very much!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:06.080
But make sure it's just this once.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.210
Are you really going to do this?

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:10.670
Yeah.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:14.470
I've done some homework and I've asked people from other schools, so I'm pretty sure that my information is correct.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.640
I really don't understand the Astronomy Club.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.680
Then let's get on with the preparations!

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.180
I-I can do the rest myself...

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.480
It's fine, really. We <i>want</i> to help.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:27.190
Yay!

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:32.780
You're really enthusiastic; I'm sure Akeno will be happy.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:34.950
I hope so.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:40.120
I didn't find out about Mihoshi's father until recently.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.450
She loved him so much; I'm sure she's affected.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.040
Yet I didn't know anything...

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:49.790
I must have said so many insensitive things.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:57.590
But Mii-chan... she said she was happy that we saw the meteor shower together.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.050
The truth is, I didn't actually see much.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.180
I was just on the phone with her.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:09.650
After hearing that, this is the only thing I <i>can</i> do.

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:11.650
Hold it!

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:11.650
Hold it!

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.570
They told us everything.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.780
Why are you here?

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:19.320
O-Ooyagi-kun, you idiot!

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.950
You idiot!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.950
We also feel the need to do something for her.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.460
If that's the case, let us join as well.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.170
Sayo-senpai! President!

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.340
So, guys, what are we going to do?

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.220
Papa, what should I do?

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:49.940
Come with me.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:50.900
What?

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:53.150
Just come with me.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:02.780
You know, Saku-chan, I'm fine.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.240
I didn't purposely try to keep my dad's death a secret...

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:10.620
The school?

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:13.840
Huh?

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.170
Are we allowed in?

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.930
Say, Saku-chan.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.440
We don't have much time, let's start.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.320
Fumin... all of you...

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.030
Huh?

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:43.410
It might not look like it, but this is a meteor shower stargazing group.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.790
This time, we can watch them together properly.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.750
Did you forget because of the exams?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.040
Today's Geminids' peak.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.000
All of you...

00:19:56.840 --> 00:20:00.720
Did you all prepare this in secret?

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:01.720
I'm sorry.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.390
This was the only thing I could think of to cheer you up...

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:14.190
Mihoshi.

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:14.900
Mii-chan.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:19.900
I was lonely... I was really lonely...

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.990
What should I do...

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.360
Don't cry. We didn't want you to be disappointed if the weather was bad.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:26.490
I'm sorry. I know this isn't enough, but...

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.370
You're an old woman, why are you crying so much?!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:32.960
Look! We can stargaze while sitting in the kotatsu eating mandarins.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.770
Papa, everyone held a stargazing session for me.

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:53.390
They all wanted to stargaze together.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:58.440
Mihoshi, there are many stars out.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:02.780
I hope you'll be able to see them with your friends one day.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:10.790
21 minutes, 30 seconds. In Pollux's direction. The apparent magnitude is -2.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:11.330
Okay.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:15.000
Still, this view is out of this world.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.880
But it's warm.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:24.340
You know, Saku-chan, I was really happy to hear you mention my papa from time to time.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:28.600
It felt like my papa still lived inside of you.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:31.560
That's why... It wasn't like I was trying to keep it a secret.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.070
Everyone, let's hold hands!

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.660
Hello, Papa.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.790
How are the stars over on your side?

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.370
Wonderful. They're beautiful.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:00.670
Everyone, I love you!

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:05.340
The power of love! It's the power of love!

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:09.720
I'll tell you this again, those two aren't going out.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:10.800
What?!

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:10.760
What?!

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.780
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:30.450
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.740
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.920
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.500
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.880
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:54.180
playing with my memories

00:22:54.180 --> 00:23:00.020
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:02.980
Into the future,

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:11.530
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.950
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:21.040
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:29.970
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.140
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:40.390
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:47.190
Next time, on Sora no Manimani:

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:49.150
Like White Snow.

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:50.070
I'm freezing!
